 "notes": "Stage-2 predicts the open->close move of the fair line in points; tiers are |predicted move| thresholds. PROVEN = passed every pre-set holdout criterion; LEAN = best candidate, NOT proven. Close = nflverse closing consensus line; open = ESPN Opening (2014-16) / ESPN BET or DraftKings open (2023+). CAVEATS: the totals pass is driven mostly by 2016; on 2023-25 book opens alone it is positive but not significant (see era_split); with every feature lagged one game the totals edge is not significant (lag1_sensitivity), so it depends on the open being posted after the previous game. Verify live with the app's own first-seen price before trusting it. REPLICATION (external_evidence, evidence only, no refit): on the owner's AusSportsBetting openers 2017-22, seasons the research never had an opener for, the totals rule |pred move| >= 1.0 gave 416 bets, CLV EV +3.47%, Bonferroni p < 0.001, positive in 6/6 seasons; on the designated 2019+2021 holdout +1.74% (n=122, p = 0.019 raw, 0.27 Bonferroni). These openers are UNTIMED (Pinnacle 2014-Feb 2018, bet365 after), so the open-timing caveat stands. Spreads: still UNPROVEN.",
 "external_evidence": {
  "what": "Out-of-sample replication on the owner's real NFL openers. Evidence only: nothing was fit on these openers and the stage-1/stage-2 coefficients in this file are unchanged by it (nfl/research/external_proof.py).",
